# Frame Inventory

Application for the frame-inventory take-home exercise.

## System Overview

Next.js serves the inventory and import workspace. It sends GraphQL requests through a same-origin route to the BFF, which calls Spring Boot over gRPC. Docker Compose runs these services alongside PostgreSQL, Temporal, a local S3/SQS emulator, Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Alloy, and the OpenTelemetry Collector. The exercise provides a legacy export in `data/inventory_frame.csv` and describes the inventory features in `INSTRUCTIONS.md`.

Bring the whole stack up with one command.

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Once PostgreSQL is healthy, the backend applies pending Flyway migrations during startup.
You can start the stack with no `.env` or with a copy of `.env.example`.
Open `/frames` to browse inventory or `/imports` to upload a CSV. The root URL
redirects to `/frames`. Bookmark `/imports/<jobId>` to reopen an import job and
enter the local operator token to see its results. If imports are disabled, the
Imports page explains how to enable them.

If you have `just` installed, run `just` to list the available recipes.

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `just up` | Generate a local import token if needed, then build and start the stack. |
| `just down` | Stop the stack and retain its named data volumes. |
| `just compose logs -f backend` | Pass arguments through to Docker Compose. |
| `just migrate` | Run Flyway on its own in a one-off backend container. |

## Subdirectories & System Boundaries

- [Application source](./src/README.md) contains the Spring Boot backend, Apollo Server BFF, and Next.js frontend.
- [Design system](./design-system/README.md) contains the prototype, sample frame data, and visual conventions for the exercise.

## Design Decisions & Trade-offs

### Scope
'use client'

import Link from 'next/link'
import { usePathname } from 'next/navigation'
import { createContext, useContext, useState, type ReactElement, type ReactNode } from 'react'
import { FrameDialog } from './frame-dialog'

type OpenFrameDialog = (frameId: string | undefined, onSaved: (id: string) => void) => void
type ImportToken = REDACTED token: string; setToken: (token: string) => void }

const FrameDialogContext = createContext<OpenFrameDialog | null>(null)
const ImportTokenContext = createContext<ImportToken | null>(null)

export function useFrameDialog(): OpenFrameDialog {
  const openFrameDialog = useContext(FrameDialogContext)
  if (!openFrameDialog) throw new Error('The frame dialog requires the inventory workspace.')
  return openFrameDialog
}

export function useImportToken(): ImportToken {
  const importToken = useContext(ImportTokenContext)
  if (!importToken) throw new Error('Import authorization requires the inventory workspace.')
  return importToken
}

export function InventoryWorkspace({ children }: { children: ReactNode }): ReactElement {
  const pathname = usePathname()
  const [token, setToken] = useState('')
  const [frameDialog, setFrameDialog] = useState<{
    frameId: string | undefined
    pathname: string
    onSaved: (id: string) => void
  } | null>(null)

  if (frameDialog && frameDialog.pathname !== pathname) setFrameDialog(null)

  return (
    <FrameDialogContext.Provider value={(frameId, onSaved) => setFrameDialog({ frameId, pathname, onSaved })}>
      <ImportTokenContext.Provider value={{ token, setToken }}>
        <div className="workspace">
          <header className="workspace-rail">
            <div className="product">
              <span className="product-mark" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="1.8">
                  <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="1" />
                  <path d="M3 9h18" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              Frame Inventory
            </div>
            <nav aria-label="Inventory navigation">
              <Link href="/frames" aria-current={pathname === '/frames' || pathname.startsWith('/frames/') ? 'page' : undefined}>
                Frames
              </Link>
              <Link href="/imports" aria-current={pathname === '/imports' || pathname.startsWith('/imports/') ? 'page' : undefined}>
                Imports
              </Link>
            </nav>
          </header>
          <main>{children}</main>
          {frameDialog && frameDialog.pathname === pathname && (
            <FrameDialog
              frameId={frameDialog.frameId}
              onClose={() => setFrameDialog(null)}
              onSaved={(id) => {
                setFrameDialog(null)
                frameDialog.onSaved(id)
              }}
            />
          )}
        </div>
      </ImportTokenContext.Provider>
    </FrameDialogContext.Provider>
  )
}
